From: Abdul <xizko55@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: core: no timestamp support on Toshiba THGJFJT2T85BAT0A

The Galaxy Book4 Edge's UFS part rejects the timestamp attribute, like the THGJFJT1E45BATP
already listed. Found running on this laptop's kernel (kernel-ws) on 2026-10-08 without a patch.
---
diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index a41b56dbf..98df15e22 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -321,6 +321,9 @@ static const struct ufs_dev_quirk ufs_fixups[] = {
 	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
 	  .model = "THGJFJT1E45BATP",
 	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
+	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
+	  .model = "THGJFJT2T85BAT0A",
+	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
 	{}
 };
 
